From: Tilo <noreply@tilo.so>
Subject: [PATCH] composefs: merge the staged deployment's /etc again at every finalize

Tilo finalizes a staged deployment right after staging, so that a machine
that loses power instead of shutting down still boots the update, and again
at shutdown. The /etc merge was made only by the finalize that exchanged the
boot loader entries, so whatever /etc became after staging (a connection, an
account, a unit drop-in) was missing in the deployment that booted next. And
the merge wrote into the deployment's etc itself, so a second merge into its
result would have kept a file deleted since the first.

Now every finalize of a staged deployment merges its /etc again, from the
staged image's own /etc, and exchanges the entries only while they are still
staged. The merge is built beside the deployment's etc as etc.next, synced to
disk and exchanged with etc in one rename, so a power loss at any point
leaves the previous merge or the new one, each whole. Staging lays the image's
/etc down with the same copy.
